# UI Layering Precedence

Before adding or moving floating UI, check the stacking order. Prefer existing layers over inventing new z-index values.

## Layer Order

- Base content and map: default / `z-0`.
- Mobile list drawer: around `z-[1090]`.
- Quick filter rail: around `z-[1100]`.
- Search top bar and its nudges: around `z-[1200]` to `z-[1400]`.
- Map listing popups: around `z-[1300]`.
- App chrome dropdowns (avatar menu, notification menu): around `z-[1800]` to `z-[1850]`.
- Sheets and app modals, including sign-in/sign-up: `z-[2000]` to `z-[2100]`.
- Confirmation dialogs: `z-[2200]`.

## Rules

- Header/avatar/notification menus must appear above search filters, map overlays, nudges, and rails.
- Sign-in/sign-up must appear above search filters, map overlays, avatar menus, and app chrome.
- Search nudges must appear above the map and not be clipped by parent overflow.
- Do not raise page controls above modals.
- When an element is still hidden despite a high child z-index, inspect parent stacking contexts (`position`, `z-index`, `transform`, `opacity`, `overflow`) before increasing the child value.
- Avoid `overflow-hidden` on containers that need tooltips, nudges, dropdowns, or pulse rings to escape.
